{
  "info": {
    "name": "ZATCA API \u2014 test site (zatca-test)",
    "_postman_id": "e2f4a6b8-1c3d-4e5f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b",
    "description": "# ZATCA API \u2014 test site\n\nPre-configured for the **`zatca-test.enfonoerp.com`** test site, seeded with company\n**ZATCA Test Co** (SAR, 15% VAT).\n\n## Before you run anything\n\n1. Select the **ZATCA API \u2014 test site** environment.\n2. Paste `api_key` and `api_secret`. They are deliberately blank in the repo and are never\n   committed. An operator with bench access can reissue a pair by re-running the seeder; the\n   secret is only recoverable at creation, so a re-run issues a new one.\n3. Run **01 Ping**. Everything else assumes it passed.\n\n`base_url` is already set to `https://zatca-test.enfonoerp.com`, which works over public\nHTTPS \u2014 there is nothing to tunnel or forward. A second environment\n(`..._tunnel.postman_environment.json`) exists for reaching the app server directly when the\nproxy layer itself is what is under investigation; it needs a port-forward that an operator\nsets up, and it relies on the `X-Frappe-Site-Name` header every request already carries.\n\n## Run them in order\n\nLater requests reuse `external_id` and the invoice names captured by earlier ones. Some\nrequests are **meant** to fail \u2014 they prove the error handling.\n\n## Expected numbers on this site\n\n| Request | Expect |\n| --- | --- |\n| dry run | net 500, VAT 75, grand **575 SAR**, `valid: true` |\n| B2B no address | `valid: false`, the missing address parts named |\n| B2C create | grand **575**, QR returned |\n| B2B create | grand **5175**, warnings empty |\n| mixed VAT | net 2000, VAT **150** (not 300) |\n| three VAT categories | net 3000, VAT **150**, grand **3150** |\n| credit note | `is_return: 1`, negative quantities, `return_reason` echoed |\n\nFull reference: `docs/USER_GUIDE.md`. Spec for whoever builds the feed:\n`docs/DATA_CONTRACT.md`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "apikey",
    "apikey": [
      {
        "key": "key",
        "value": "Authorization",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "value",
        "value": "token {{api_key}}:{{api_secret}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "in",
        "value": "header",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const pad = n => String(n).padStart(2, \"0\");",
          "const fmt = d => `${d.getFullYear()}-${pad(d.getMonth() + 1)}-${pad(d.getDate())}`;",
          "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get(\"posting_date\")) {",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"posting_date\", fmt(new Date()));",
          "}",
          "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get(\"external_id\")) {",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"external_id\", \"PM-\" + Date.now());",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "external_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "last_invoice",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "last_qr_png",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "posting_date",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 Ping \u2014 run this first",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "token {{api_key}}:{{api_secret}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "X-Frappe-Site-Name",
            "value": "{{site_name}}",
            "description": "Only needed when base_url is an IP or a tunnel; ignored otherwise."
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/method/zatca_api.api.v1.ping",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "method",
            "zatca_api.api.v1.ping"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Confirms the key pair works, the custom fields are migrated, and which ZATCA phase the seeded company resolves to.\n\nOn this test site expect: `custom_fields_installed: true`, `ksa_compliance 0.58.0`, and `ZATCA Test Co -> Phase 1`.\n\nIf this fails with 403, check `api_key` / `api_secret` in the environment. If it fails with \"App zatca_api is not installed\", `base_url` is reaching a different site on the same server \u2014 see the collection description."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test(\"envelope present\", () => pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"message\"));",
              "const env = body.message;",
              "pm.test(\"success = true\", () => pm.expect(env.success, JSON.stringify(env.errors)).to.be.true);",
              "",
              "const d = env.data;",
              "pm.test(\"custom fields migrated\", () => pm.expect(d.custom_fields_installed).to.be.true);",
              "console.log(\"site:\", d.site, \"| app version:\", d.version, \"| submit_mode:\", d.submit_mode);",
              "const r = d.readiness;",
              "console.log(\"ksa_compliance:\", r.ksa_compliance_installed, r.ksa_compliance_version);",
              "(r.companies || []).forEach(c => console.log(\"   \", c.company, \"->\", c.phase));",
              "pm.test(\"seeded company present\", () =>",
              "    pm.expect((r.companies || []).map(c => c.company)).to.include(\"{{company}}\"));",
              ""
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
